# local analysis / planning docs (not for commit). Plans do not go in git: they
# rot against the code and then read as authoritative. Markdown elsewhere is
# ignored by default and re-included by explicit exception below.
*.md
# The exceptions are the documents that describe the project to an outsider
# rather than planning its future. Both are anchored with a leading slash so
# they match at the root only.
!/README.md
!/SECURITY.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
# docs/ is TRACKED: the guide and the reference describe the shipped API, and
# an untracked docs/ is a fresh clone whose README points at nothing.
!/docs/**/*.md
# Planning/audit reports under docs/report/ are local analysis, not shipped
# reference docs -- re-ignored after the negation above (later rules win).
/docs/report/
# `bench/` is local reports and scratch -- EXCEPT the code graph, which
# CLAUDE.md tells every session to run and which only existed on one machine.
# `bench/` with a trailing slash excludes the directory, and a negation cannot
# re-include a file whose parent is excluded; `bench/*` excludes the contents
# instead, which a negation can override.
bench/*
!bench/codegraph.py

# local tooling (agent worktrees, settings)
.claude/

# libFuzzer target binaries (build artifacts)
# Fuzz binaries build to the repo ROOT. A PATTERN, not a list: the list
# was 14 names and already missed fuzz_dataframe. Sources live in
# src/fuzz/, so a root anchor cannot touch them.
/fuzz_*

# vendored external experiments (mimalloc, etc.)
third_party/

# PGO artifacts
pgo-data/
pgo.profdata

# macOS Finder metadata
.DS_Store
*.dSYM/

# Fuzzer and crash artefacts. libFuzzer writes a reproducer into the CWD on every
# finding, and a fault-injection run produces one per injected bug -- reproducers
# for defects that do not exist, which is worse than noise once committed. The
# corpus is regenerated by running the target and is not a source input.
crash-*
leak-*
timeout-*
oom-*
slow-unit-*
fuzz-*.log
*.profraw
*.profdata

# Core dumps and OS crash reports
# Anchored: an unanchored `core` also matches the DIRECTORY src/core/, so every
# new file added there was silently unaddable. core.* still catches numbered
# dumps at any depth.
/core
core.*
vgcore.*
*.crash
*.ips
*.dmp

# Working changelog: a running record of what landed and what it measured.
# Gitignored on purpose -- the commit messages are the shared history; this is
# the scratch that feeds them.
CHANGELOG.local.md
.build-variant
test-tls
test-aio-tls

# python bytecode cache from the pty test harness
__pycache__/

# Session scratch: PoC scripts and audit artefacts. Neither tracked nor
# ignored before, so `git status` showed residue a sweep could commit.
tmp_audit/
.opencode/
.swarm/
